Subject: Backport published socket, Phar, GIF and ctype fixes to PHP 5.6
CVE: CVE-2025-1220, CVE-2026-7260, CVE-2026-9672, CVE-2026-7258
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/cac8f7f1cf4939f55f06b68120040f057682d89c
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/2e0fa0a44441d74bf8cc4e1ce1c8af9cd4209f52
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/fcd691b377d02285740744bee17c0f298be227d5
Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/8bdee7e4c6f4e92f9e89841d53855d9ffbdbfe54

Based on the published Freexian PHP 7.0 patches. Retain PHP 5.6 long port
formatting, char-pointer error strings, hash-table lookup and TSRMLS APIs.
The ctype changes cover core and enabled extensions, preserving native
buffer members and generated scanner counterparts. Disabled extensions,
SAPIs and standalone Windows sources are omitted. Published network and
Phar assertions are unchanged; the three tar fixtures retain their bytes.

